1
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:08,510
A ride at a theme park has a sign.

2
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:12,090
You must be taller than 120 centimetres.

3
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:15,750
Lily is exactly 120 centimetres tall.

4
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,300
Can she go on the ride?

5
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:20,530
Pause the video and decide.

6
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:22,050
The answer is no.

7
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:25,270
Taller than 120 means more than 120.

8
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,140
Exactly 120 is not enough.

9
00:00:28,190 --> 00:00:31,180
But 120 and a half centimetres is fine.

10
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:36,420
In maths we write the rule like this: h is greater than 120.

11
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,640
This sign means is less than.

12
00:00:38,690 --> 00:00:40,500
3 is less than 8.

13
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:42,850
This sign means is greater than.

14
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,860
8 is greater than 3.

15
00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:48,120
The open side always faces the bigger number.

16
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:52,870
With negative numbers, negative 4 is less than negative 1.

17
00:00:52,920 --> 00:01:00,000
An inequality like h is greater than 120 describes a whole range of values, not just one.

18
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:04,350
h could be 121, or 130, or 120 and a half.

19
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,870
But not 120 itself.

20
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:13,390
On a number line, draw an open circle at 120, because 120 is not included.

21
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:18,010
Then draw an arrow to the right, towards the bigger numbers.

22
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:18,720
Your turn.

23
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:22,200
Which number satisfies x is less than negative 2?

24
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:25,520
Pause the video and choose.

25
00:01:25,570 --> 00:01:30,850
Less than negative 2 means to the left of negative 2 on the number line.

26
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:34,880
Negative 5 is to the left, so negative 5 works.

27
00:01:34,930 --> 00:01:37,090
You can join two inequalities.

28
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:41,500
This one says x is greater than negative 1, and less than 4.

29
00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:44,480
So x is between negative 1 and 4.

30
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:48,150
Draw open circles at both ends, and join them.

31
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:52,990
If x must be an integer, the possible values are 0, 1, 2 and 3.

32
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:56,150
Negative 1 and 4 are not included.

33
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,470
Here is the method.

34
00:01:57,520 --> 00:02:03,410
Step 1: decide whether the letter is greater than, or less than, the boundary.

35
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:09,000
Step 2: draw an open circle at the boundary, because it is not included.

36
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:12,460
Step 3: draw the line towards the values that work.

37
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:15,930
Right for greater than, left for less than.

38
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:20,870
Step 4: when you list integers, leave out the boundary values.

39
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:23,590
Write an inequality for this sentence.

40
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:27,640
The temperature, t, was below negative 3 degrees.

41
00:02:27,690 --> 00:02:29,220
Below means less than.

42
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:31,860
So t is less than negative 3.

43
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:33,420
Now read a number line.

44
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:37,780
There is an open circle at 1, and an arrow to the right.

45
00:02:37,830 --> 00:02:40,670
The open circle means 1 is not included.

46
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:43,190
The arrow points to bigger numbers.

47
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,400
So x is greater than 1.

48
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:51,210
List the integers that satisfy negative 3 is less than x, is less than 2.

49
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:55,200
x is greater than negative 3, so start at negative 2.

50
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:57,780
Negative 3 is not included.

51
00:02:57,830 --> 00:03:00,680
x is less than 2, so stop at 1.

52
00:03:00,730 --> 00:03:05,170
The integers are negative 2, negative 1, 0 and 1.

53
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:05,880
Your turn.

54
00:03:05,930 --> 00:03:10,700
How many integers satisfy negative 2 is less than x, is less than 3?

55
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:13,590
Pause and count them.

56
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:17,670
Start just after negative 2, and stop just before 3.

57
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:20,810
The integers are negative 1, 0, 1 and 2.

58
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:22,850
That is 4 integers.

59
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:25,560
Sometimes the letter is on the right.

60
00:03:25,610 --> 00:03:27,650
10 is greater than y.

61
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:30,100
Read it starting from the letter.

62
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:33,660
If 10 is greater than y, then y is less than 10.

63
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:36,060
They mean the same thing.

64
00:03:36,110 --> 00:03:41,070
Finn lists the integers that satisfy 4 is less than x, is less than 8.

65
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:43,620
Which line goes wrong first?

66
00:03:43,670 --> 00:03:44,840
Line 2 is wrong.

67
00:03:44,890 --> 00:03:48,630
4 is not greater than 4, and 8 is not less than 8.

68
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:51,610
The end values are not included.

69
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:53,940
The integers are 5, 6 and 7.

70
00:03:53,990 --> 00:03:56,060
That is 3 integers.

71
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:58,240
Inequalities are all around you.

72
00:03:58,290 --> 00:04:03,890
A speed limit sign means your speed must not be more than the number shown.

73
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:10,080
A lift that carries fewer than 8 people: the number of people, p, is less than 8.

74
00:04:10,130 --> 00:04:14,560
And water is liquid between its freezing and boiling points.

75
00:04:14,610 --> 00:04:19,290
At sea level, that is between 0 and 100 degrees Celsius.

76
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,620
One last question.

77
00:04:20,670 --> 00:04:23,140
The integer n can be 1, 2, 3 or 4.

78
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:25,370
Which inequality describes it?

79
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:28,770
Pause the video and choose.

80
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:32,330
n must be greater than 0, so that it starts at 1.

81
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:35,170
And less than 5, so that it stops at 4.

82
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:39,130
The answer is 0 is less than n, is less than 5.

83
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:42,310
To remember: x greater than a, or x less than a.

84
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:45,170
The value a itself is not included.

85
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:51,750
On a number line, draw an open circle at the boundary, and a line towards the values that work.

86
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:55,800
A double inequality means x is between two values.

87
00:04:55,850 --> 00:05:00,020
When you list integers, leave out the boundary values.

88
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:05,190
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.6 on Camday.
